TI  - Generation of mWasabi fluorescent protein-binding nanobodies.
AB  - mWasabi is a bright monomeric green fluorescent protein. It can be used as a fusion tag to monitor various biological events, e.g. protein localization. Here we report the selection of camelid-derived single-domain antibody fragments (nanobodies) against mWasabi. In this work, phage-display approach was employed to select the high affinity mWasabi-specific Nb (nanobodies). These nanobodies were able to recognize mWasabi or in a fused fashion with PD1. The interesting binding characteristics of these two mWasabi-specific nanobodies could be valuable for design new tools for cellular tracing or targeting based on the mWasabi-fusing protein in many different biological research fields.
